Z||000001||batboy||02-26-2000||06:43 PM||||Whew! It's been a confusing weekend already, Paul! They (my friends) are not moving this weekend, it'll have to be next weekend, something because the lease begins the first of the month, but they thought that they were going to get to slide in a couple days early. Guess not! The former tenants are late or something. I'll call ahead of time, Paul. Maybe next weekend. I did get the clutch work done on my 85 GT today, yippee! I cruised to Emporia and did some shopping. The clutch works like a charm, thanks in part to Rodney Dickman and a couple of his parts.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 02-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||02-26-2000||07:42 PM||||Batboy,<P>Well, I have been busy while not waiting for you!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I have my 3.1 almost together for the GT and have been working on finishing up the Coupe.  I am trying to get the Quad 4's Isuzu 5 speed's clutch slave to work with the Fiero's master cylinder.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>If Fiero people think bleeding the slave on the Fieros is a pain, try the TwinCam Sunfire's Isuzu slave!  There isn't a bleed screw!!!!  You have to fill the slave with brake fluid and then bleed the open line and somewhere there, join the two before air gets in!  <P>I tried (I really did!) to do the above but when I tried to mount the slave cylinder to the transaxle, I couldn't push the slave cylinder in far enough to start the hold down nuts!  Looks like I got to take the line off again, push the slave cylinder on to the transaxle (spraying brake fluid everywhere!!) and then put the line back on the slave WITHOUT getting any air into the system.  <P>Wish me luck!  The air isn't too blue ... yet!<P>BTW, It isn't a matter of not enough hands... there isn't enough room for my two, let alone another set.<P>Paul||||reg||1
